WEBVTT

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:08.958
"The idol group"

00:00:09.208 --> 00:00:10.958
"everyone's watching"

00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:15.417
The members of Six Gravity and Procellarum,
groups who suddenly shot to stardom,

00:00:15.417 --> 00:00:17.542
are here at our studio today!

00:00:19.333 --> 00:00:21.583
Thank you for coming.

00:00:21.583 --> 00:00:28.667
Please introduce yourselves, starting
with the leader of Six Gravity, Hajime.

00:00:28.667 --> 00:00:31.250
Hello, my name is Hajime Mutsuki.

00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:33.292
Thank you for having us today.

00:00:33.292 --> 00:00:36.667
I am Haru Yayoi, also from Six Gravity.

00:00:36.667 --> 00:00:40.917
We'll work hard so that people can
learn a little more about us today.

00:00:40.917 --> 00:00:44.208
I'm Arata Uduki. Nice to meet ya.

00:00:44.208 --> 00:00:45.708
I am Aoi Satsuki.

00:00:45.708 --> 00:00:48.167
Nice to meet you, everyone.

00:00:48.167 --> 00:00:51.625
Hello! I'm Koi Kisaragi. Call me "Koi"!

00:00:51.625 --> 00:00:55.042
I'm Kakeru Shiwasu! Nice to meet you!

00:00:55.042 --> 00:00:59.833
Next up is Procellarum,
starting with their leader, Shun.

00:00:59.833 --> 00:01:02.083
Hey, everyone, good afternoon.

00:01:02.083 --> 00:01:04.667
I am the white demon king of Procellarum.

00:01:04.667 --> 00:01:08.042
Just kidding. I'm the leader, Shun Shimotsuki.

00:01:08.042 --> 00:01:09.833
Nice to meet you.

00:01:09.833 --> 00:01:12.167
I am Kai Fuduki from Procellarum.

00:01:12.167 --> 00:01:14.542
We'll work hard so we won't lose to Gravi.

00:01:14.542 --> 00:01:17.250
Yoo-hoo! I am You Haduki from Procellarum.

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:20.083
We're waiting for your support! Mwah!

00:01:20.083 --> 00:01:22.125
I-It's hard to follow that...

00:01:22.125 --> 00:01:24.292
Hello, I am Yoru Nagatsuki.

00:01:24.292 --> 00:01:28.208
I will do my best. Please support us!

00:01:28.208 --> 00:01:29.708
I'm Rui Minaduki.

00:01:29.708 --> 00:01:30.875
Nice to meet you.

00:01:30.875 --> 00:01:32.583
I'm Iku Kannaduki!

00:01:32.583 --> 00:01:36.167
I'll give it my all! Please support us!

00:01:36.167 --> 00:01:41.583
After the commercial, we'll give you more
details about both up-and-coming groups!

00:01:42.542 --> 00:01:44.958
"Music video for new song after the break"

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:47.292
♪ Shakin', sugar, sugar! ♪

00:01:47.292 --> 00:01:49.292
♪ Shakin', sugar, sugar! ♪

00:01:50.708 --> 00:01:53.292
--♪ Shake it love, YES! ♪
--Quickly rising in popularity,

00:01:53.292 --> 00:01:56.208
all eyes are on where they go from here!

00:01:56.208 --> 00:01:58.167
Do your best from here on out, too.

00:01:58.167 --> 00:02:00.167
Thank you very much!

00:02:00.167 --> 00:02:02.208
Now, do you have any announcements?

00:02:02.208 --> 00:02:05.375
Yes, we're having a
handshake event this afternoon.

00:02:05.375 --> 00:02:08.292
If you get a chance, please come!

00:02:08.292 --> 00:02:10.208
--Yay!
--We'll be performing a new song, too!

00:02:10.208 --> 00:02:11.625
Look forward to it!

00:02:11.625 --> 00:02:13.375
Look, I was talking about this!

00:02:13.375 --> 00:02:13.667
No.

00:02:13.667 --> 00:02:14.292
"#01: Betting on the Handshake Event!"
No.

00:02:14.292 --> 00:02:16.042
"#01: Betting on the Handshake Event!"
There's no way.

00:02:16.042 --> 00:02:19.042
Syunpei, please! I'll never
ask you for anything again!

00:02:19.042 --> 00:02:22.250
Please go to today's event for me!

00:02:22.250 --> 00:02:24.708
You don't have to actually shake his hand.

00:02:24.708 --> 00:02:29.750
Just get the merch that's only available
at the handshake event for me. Please!

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:32.042
Eh, don't wanna.

00:02:32.042 --> 00:02:36.458
It's so lame that you got a
fever at a time like this, Sis.

00:02:36.458 --> 00:02:39.667
I know that without you telling me.

00:02:39.667 --> 00:02:43.000
But I thought, "I should learn
the dance for their new song,"

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:44.417
and then fell asleep...

00:02:44.417 --> 00:02:46.792
Of course you'd get sick if you didn't
dry your hair after taking a bath

00:02:46.792 --> 00:02:49.792
and then fall asleep with the AC on.

00:02:49.792 --> 00:02:52.000
It's important to remember the dance!

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:54.292
If everyone else around me
is waving their lights properly,

00:02:54.292 --> 00:02:57.292
I'll stand out if I'm
the only one who messes up.

00:02:57.292 --> 00:03:00.292
I want to cheer on everyone on stage!

00:03:00.292 --> 00:03:05.083
Aw man, Mom and Dad finally let me go to
a handshake event after I started high school.

00:03:05.083 --> 00:03:10.417
Aw, but now I can't meet Kakerun anymore!

00:03:10.417 --> 00:03:11.542
Kakerun?

00:03:11.542 --> 00:03:14.250
Kakerun is a member of Six Gravity.

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:16.833
He's the best!

00:03:16.833 --> 00:03:20.625
Kakerun. Real name:
Kakeru Shiwasu. 16 years old.

00:03:20.625 --> 00:03:24.917
He's always cheerful and energetic,
and he has a dreamy smile.

00:03:24.917 --> 00:03:29.917
Often paired with Kakerun
is Koikku, or Koi Kisaragi.

00:03:29.917 --> 00:03:31.875
There are some parts of him that are unfortunate,

00:03:31.875 --> 00:03:36.167
but he and Kakerun make things lively in Gravi.

00:03:36.167 --> 00:03:39.417
These two are called the "junior pair."

00:03:39.417 --> 00:03:43.500
Arata and Prince Aoi are a year older
and called the "middle pair."

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:47.208
Oh, those two will be in a play soon, too.

00:03:47.208 --> 00:03:50.333
Last are the two oldest, the "senior pair!"

00:03:50.333 --> 00:03:52.125
King Hajime and Haru!

00:03:52.125 --> 00:03:56.417
Haru is smart and kind,
like everyone's big brother.

00:03:56.417 --> 00:04:02.375
The leader, King Hajime, is Gravi's
flawless king, and super charismatic!

00:04:02.375 --> 00:04:04.708
Sis, don't you have a fever?

00:04:04.708 --> 00:04:07.958
Yeah, that's right.

00:04:07.958 --> 00:04:10.875
Aw man, I can't go on any longer. I can't.

00:04:10.875 --> 00:04:14.292
This might your big sister's last request.

00:04:14.292 --> 00:04:15.708
Please, Syunpei.

00:04:15.708 --> 00:04:19.625
You can buy those sweets you said
you wanted to eat while you're there, too.

00:04:22.458 --> 00:04:24.792
Jeez. All right already.

00:04:24.792 --> 00:04:27.792
Thank you, dear brother!

00:04:27.792 --> 00:04:28.875
Get off of me!

00:04:28.875 --> 00:04:30.708
You're gonna get me sick!

00:04:30.708 --> 00:04:32.875
Oh, no! That definitely can't happen!

00:04:32.875 --> 00:04:35.583
If Kakerun gets sick because
of me, that'll be terrible!

00:04:35.583 --> 00:04:39.458
But if my cold goes into Kakerun's body...

00:04:39.458 --> 00:04:41.000
--No...! What'll I do if that happens?!

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:42.458
--Well, I'm off then.
--No...! What'll I do if that happens?!

00:04:42.458 --> 00:04:46.292
Wait, I need to give you the map
and money, and the ticket for the event!

00:04:55.375 --> 00:04:58.208
What the heck?
I can't tell where to go at all.

00:04:58.750 --> 00:05:02.333
Oh, wow! We're finally getting
to see Hajime in person!

00:05:03.917 --> 00:05:06.750
Oh, this is like the one Sis had in her room.

00:05:12.958 --> 00:05:14.792
Who are you looking for?

00:05:19.125 --> 00:05:21.708
♪ Shake it love, YES! ♪

00:05:25.042 --> 00:05:26.125
Be careful.

00:05:26.125 --> 00:05:27.833
Thank you very much!

00:05:27.833 --> 00:05:29.167
Okay, thanks.

00:05:29.167 --> 00:05:30.792
Good work!

00:05:32.833 --> 00:05:36.250
Our timing's still off for our
arm movements in the chorus.

00:05:36.250 --> 00:05:39.917
Pay attention to who's next to you
and make sure you're together.

00:05:39.917 --> 00:05:42.667
It'll look uncool if we mess this part up.

00:05:42.667 --> 00:05:43.542
Yes, sir!

00:05:43.542 --> 00:05:46.292
We return to our first side line
formation from the pre-chorus,

00:05:46.292 --> 00:05:48.333
so make sure we're spread out evenly.

00:05:48.333 --> 00:05:51.250
Especially Kakeru and Koi.
You two end up closer than the rest of us.

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:53.000
Yes, sir!

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:56.208
Let's check it together later.

00:05:56.208 --> 00:05:58.208
Just because it's the first
performance of our new song

00:05:58.208 --> 00:06:00.625
doesn't mean we can dance
with anything less than our best.

00:06:00.625 --> 00:06:03.417
Don't give an embarrassing performance.

00:06:03.417 --> 00:06:04.708
We won't!

00:06:04.708 --> 00:06:08.125
They'll be setting up the stage
for a while after this,

00:06:08.125 --> 00:06:10.750
so we have a break until they call us.

00:06:10.750 --> 00:06:14.333
Please review the flow of what
we're doing for the event as you rest.

00:06:14.333 --> 00:06:15.750
Okay.

00:06:21.125 --> 00:06:22.542
All right.

00:06:25.917 --> 00:06:27.208
Hajime?

00:06:27.208 --> 00:06:28.625
Yes?

00:06:30.167 --> 00:06:32.667
Do you have a moment?

00:06:32.667 --> 00:06:34.083
Yes.

00:06:40.583 --> 00:06:43.125
Shun, can you come with me for a bit?

00:06:43.125 --> 00:06:45.333
We're having a meeting in a different room.

00:06:45.333 --> 00:06:46.750
Okay.

00:06:53.208 --> 00:06:55.833
Oh, Shun was the only one called?

00:06:55.833 --> 00:06:57.083
Hajime, too?

00:06:57.083 --> 00:07:01.042
Yeah. Our manager, Mr. Tsukishiro,
just came and got him.

00:07:01.042 --> 00:07:05.125
Oh? The two leaders were called into
a meeting? I wonder what's going on.

00:07:05.125 --> 00:07:08.542
I wonder. It might be something big.

00:07:08.542 --> 00:07:10.958
Oh, yeah, maybe.

00:07:10.958 --> 00:07:12.958
Can you read this word?

00:07:12.958 --> 00:07:14.458
Hm? Which one?

00:07:14.458 --> 00:07:16.167
You couldn't look it up?

00:07:16.167 --> 00:07:20.458
It's blurry, so I can't make out the whole thing.

00:07:20.458 --> 00:07:23.583
Let's see... where's my
electronic dictionary...

00:07:24.708 --> 00:07:26.333
Isn't that "crescent moon"?

00:07:26.333 --> 00:07:27.917
Oh, thanks.

00:07:27.917 --> 00:07:31.292
That's Yoru the bookworm for you.

00:07:31.292 --> 00:07:34.708
Do you know the dance for your new song?

00:07:34.708 --> 00:07:38.958
Well, I remember all the moves,
but that's about it.

00:07:38.958 --> 00:07:40.292
Practice makes perfect!

00:07:41.333 --> 00:07:43.208
Do your best.

00:07:43.208 --> 00:07:44.958
Easy for you to say, Iku.

00:07:44.958 --> 00:07:47.375
You're lucky that you're good at dancing.

00:07:47.375 --> 00:07:49.250
That's not true.

00:07:51.792 --> 00:07:54.000
Kakeru, what's that?

00:07:55.333 --> 00:07:58.500
The specialty sweets for this area
that are near the event space!

00:07:58.500 --> 00:08:01.292
I've wanted to try them for a while!

00:08:01.292 --> 00:08:03.500
Look, like this!

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:06.083
Oh, that's cute.

00:08:06.083 --> 00:08:07.542
Right?

00:08:08.500 --> 00:08:09.917
Excuse me.

00:08:16.458 --> 00:08:19.750
Sorry to call you out right before the event,

00:08:19.750 --> 00:08:23.083
but there is something
we would like to tell you two.

00:08:26.750 --> 00:08:28.167
President?

00:08:31.292 --> 00:08:33.917
Now, let us begin the meeting.

00:08:36.667 --> 00:08:39.042
This looks like the right place,

00:08:39.042 --> 00:08:42.417
but how am I supposed to
shake hands and get the merch?

00:08:42.417 --> 00:08:44.958
There is still time before the doors open.

00:08:44.958 --> 00:08:46.583
Gathering here will create an obstruction,

00:08:46.583 --> 00:08:48.417
--so please meet somewhere else.

00:08:48.417 --> 00:08:49.750
--Is he lost?
--so please meet somewhere else.

00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:51.417
Maybe he came with his mom?

00:08:51.417 --> 00:08:54.000
I wonder if he's someone's fan?

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:56.208
Oh, he's so cute!

00:09:00.958 --> 00:09:02.458
"Authorized Personel Only"

00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:09.000
Excuse me...

00:09:10.333 --> 00:09:11.667
I'll just go in!

00:09:11.667 --> 00:09:13.667
Wait, maybe this isn't it...

00:09:19.417 --> 00:09:20.833
Oh, shoot!

00:09:32.333 --> 00:09:34.250
Ow...

00:09:34.250 --> 00:09:36.208
Are you okay?

00:09:36.208 --> 00:09:38.000
Are you hurt?

00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:39.208
Sorry.

00:09:39.208 --> 00:09:41.250
Oh, I'm fine.

00:09:43.083 --> 00:09:45.083
Who are you?

00:09:45.083 --> 00:09:48.208
Um... I got a little lost...

00:09:48.208 --> 00:09:49.917
Lost, huh?

00:09:49.917 --> 00:09:52.333
Only authorized people can come in here.

00:09:56.125 --> 00:09:58.583
Where were you trying to go, little boy?

00:09:58.583 --> 00:10:00.833
Don't call me a little boy!

00:10:00.833 --> 00:10:02.917
My name's Syunpei.

00:10:02.917 --> 00:10:04.542
Sorry, Syunpei.

00:10:04.542 --> 00:10:07.083
So, where did you want to go?

00:10:07.083 --> 00:10:10.208
I heard that the Gravi
handshake event was here,

00:10:10.208 --> 00:10:13.750
but how can I get a handshake, Mr. Staff?

00:10:13.750 --> 00:10:15.125
Staff?

00:10:15.125 --> 00:10:18.250
Sis told me to go to the handshake event--

00:10:18.250 --> 00:10:20.833
she said I didn't have to shake hands,

00:10:20.833 --> 00:10:25.000
but I better bring home
the special merch, or else!

00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:27.583
Whose hand did you want to shake from Gravi?

00:10:27.583 --> 00:10:30.125
"Kakero"... I think?

00:10:30.125 --> 00:10:31.417
"Kokeru" maybe?

00:10:31.417 --> 00:10:32.542
Yeah, that one!

00:10:32.542 --> 00:10:33.958
It's "Kakeru"!

00:10:33.958 --> 00:10:35.833
Oh yeah, that one!

00:10:35.833 --> 00:10:39.708
I see. You must love your sister, Syunpei.

00:10:39.708 --> 00:10:44.083
That's not it. It's just crazy at home.

00:10:44.083 --> 00:10:48.292
When Sis bought the new CD,
she listened to it so much on repeat

00:10:48.292 --> 00:10:51.000
that I practically have it memorized.

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:53.167
Oh, you can sing it?

00:10:53.167 --> 00:10:57.208
♪ Good love! Good love! Gravity love! ♪

00:10:58.583 --> 00:11:00.167
That's pretty good!

00:11:00.167 --> 00:11:03.083
You might've learned it faster than Kakeru.

00:11:03.083 --> 00:11:04.500
Koi...

00:11:05.625 --> 00:11:07.375
As expected of one of the staff.

00:11:07.375 --> 00:11:09.958
You really know Kakeru well, huh?

00:11:11.042 --> 00:11:12.250
About the handshake event--

00:11:12.250 --> 00:11:13.875
Did you bring a ticket?

00:11:13.875 --> 00:11:14.083
"Kakeru Shiwasu"

00:11:14.083 --> 00:11:15.500
"Kakeru Shiwasu"
Yeah, here.

00:11:16.708 --> 00:11:19.000
This is the handshake event
ticket for today, huh?

00:11:19.000 --> 00:11:20.875
It's my first time seeing one.

00:11:20.875 --> 00:11:23.375
Yeah, as long as you have this, you'll be fine.

00:11:23.375 --> 00:11:28.083
Once it's time, wait in the line
by the entrance and go inside.

00:11:28.083 --> 00:11:31.417
In the event space, there'll be
a tent for Kakeru Shiwasu,

00:11:31.417 --> 00:11:33.750
so line up in that next.

00:11:33.750 --> 00:11:35.750
When the staff person says
to show your ticket later,

00:11:35.750 --> 00:11:39.208
you just have to hand this over,
and you'll be fine.

00:11:39.208 --> 00:11:40.375
Okay, I got it!

00:11:40.375 --> 00:11:42.625
Thanks, Mr. Staff!

00:11:42.625 --> 00:11:46.375
Do you need to buy any other merch?

00:11:46.375 --> 00:11:49.625
Sis said she wanted to pick it out
herself, so I didn't have to.

00:11:49.625 --> 00:11:53.250
But this is the only place to get
the merch from the handshake part,

00:11:53.250 --> 00:11:55.000
so she said to get that.

00:11:55.000 --> 00:11:57.417
I see. Then it should be fine.

00:11:57.417 --> 00:12:01.417
There's still some time before the handshake
event though. What'll you do till then?

00:12:01.417 --> 00:12:05.875
I brought this, so I'll play a game!

00:12:05.875 --> 00:12:07.250
Can I wait here?

00:12:07.250 --> 00:12:09.833
P-Probably not...

00:12:10.958 --> 00:12:13.083
Then I'll wait outside.

00:12:13.083 --> 00:12:15.208
Thanks, Mr. Staff!

00:12:15.208 --> 00:12:16.417
Oh, also--

00:12:16.417 --> 00:12:18.500
Do you know the store
that sells moon rabbit buns?

00:12:18.500 --> 00:12:21.708
I heard those sweets are really good sweets!

00:12:21.708 --> 00:12:23.125
Oh, that's--

00:12:23.125 --> 00:12:24.542
Do you have a minute?

00:12:24.542 --> 00:12:25.917
Oh, never mind.

00:12:25.917 --> 00:12:27.708
I don't want to keep bugging you.

00:12:27.708 --> 00:12:30.208
I'll find it myself. Later!

00:12:44.250 --> 00:12:46.750
"Tsukiutaya"

00:12:51.250 --> 00:12:52.500
"Low battery. Please recharge."

00:12:54.125 --> 00:12:56.500
Man, this sucks.

00:13:03.583 --> 00:13:05.000
Hello!

00:13:06.833 --> 00:13:10.958
Can you show us where to get those
moon rabbit buns you were talking about earlier?

00:13:10.958 --> 00:13:14.875
Yeah, we wanted to eat them, too. Right?

00:13:14.875 --> 00:13:15.833
Huh?

00:13:15.833 --> 00:13:17.333
We want to eat them, right?

00:13:19.583 --> 00:13:21.792
Yeah. I want to eat one.

00:13:23.167 --> 00:13:24.583
All right!

00:13:25.667 --> 00:13:28.792
I guess I have no choice. I'll show you!

00:13:33.917 --> 00:13:34.917
"Chinatown"
"Yokohama Chinese Restaurant"

00:13:34.917 --> 00:13:39.125
With this map, it's a little hard
to tell where it is, huh?

00:13:39.125 --> 00:13:41.667
Right? Who'd be able to tell?

00:13:42.708 --> 00:13:45.917
It's nice of you to go on
an errand for your big sister.

00:13:45.917 --> 00:13:48.292
I'm not doing it 'cause I'm nice!

00:13:48.292 --> 00:13:51.542
It's just the job of a little brother.

00:13:51.542 --> 00:13:52.792
You're a good boy.

00:13:52.792 --> 00:13:54.000
Good boy.

00:13:54.000 --> 00:13:55.458
"Moon Rabbit Buns"

00:13:55.458 --> 00:13:57.250
Oh, there it is!

00:14:00.750 --> 00:14:02.167
Here you are.

00:14:05.792 --> 00:14:06.958
It's good.

00:14:06.958 --> 00:14:13.125
Rui, I wonder if you can put a little more
feeling into your face and words.

00:14:13.125 --> 00:14:16.583
Syunpei, this is good!

00:14:16.583 --> 00:14:18.000
Right?

00:14:24.167 --> 00:14:26.417
Wanna go on that together?

00:14:26.417 --> 00:14:29.083
As thanks for telling us
about these moon rabbit buns.

00:14:30.875 --> 00:14:32.292
Yeah!

00:14:33.625 --> 00:14:35.458
Oh, he picked up!

00:14:35.458 --> 00:14:38.083
Are Kakeru and Koi with you, too?

00:14:38.083 --> 00:14:40.125
Yeah, they are.

00:14:40.125 --> 00:14:41.750
What are you doing right now?

00:14:41.750 --> 00:14:45.875
Right now... we're eating moon rabbit buns.

00:14:45.875 --> 00:14:47.083
What?

00:14:47.083 --> 00:14:49.625
A-Anyway, I'm heading your way now!

00:15:05.042 --> 00:15:09.417
It's been a while.
Don't remember them being that bad...

00:15:09.417 --> 00:15:11.917
What are you saying? Don't be a wimp.

00:15:17.208 --> 00:15:19.000
Those guys...

00:15:19.000 --> 00:15:20.833
What are they doing?

00:15:24.958 --> 00:15:26.917
Thanks for listening.

00:15:26.917 --> 00:15:30.042
Please keep the details secret for now.

00:15:30.042 --> 00:15:31.208
Yes, sir.

00:15:31.208 --> 00:15:33.208
"Photo Booth"

00:15:36.083 --> 00:15:37.833
They're opening the doors soon.

00:15:37.833 --> 00:15:39.917
Will you make it?

00:15:39.917 --> 00:15:42.000
Where are you guys right now?

00:15:44.292 --> 00:15:46.333
We're fine.

00:15:46.333 --> 00:15:48.458
We'll be back soon.

00:15:48.458 --> 00:15:49.667
What're you doing?

00:15:49.667 --> 00:15:52.000
Huh? Uh, i-i-it's...

00:15:52.000 --> 00:15:54.042
It's nothing.

00:15:56.750 --> 00:15:58.083
Thanks for today!

00:15:58.083 --> 00:16:00.000
It's almost time for the handshake event.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:02.583
Yeah, we had fun, too.

00:16:02.583 --> 00:16:04.542
Have fun at the handshake event!

00:16:04.542 --> 00:16:05.958
See you later!

00:16:07.083 --> 00:16:09.583
The handshake event will open soon.

00:16:09.583 --> 00:16:11.833
Please wait in two lines.

00:16:17.250 --> 00:16:18.750
"Kakeru Shiwasu Lane"

00:16:18.958 --> 00:16:23.958
Oh, Kakerun! I'm cheering
for you! Please do your best!

00:16:25.917 --> 00:16:28.208
Kakeru!

00:16:28.208 --> 00:16:30.333
Oh, nice to meet you!

00:16:30.333 --> 00:16:33.042
My name's Saki. Yes, Saki.

00:16:47.667 --> 00:16:48.917
Thanks for waiting!

00:16:48.917 --> 00:16:49.708
Huh?

00:16:49.708 --> 00:16:51.333
Huuuh?!

00:16:53.875 --> 00:16:56.042
Sorry for not telling you.

00:16:56.042 --> 00:16:57.417
I'm Kakeru.

00:16:57.417 --> 00:17:00.083
Kakeru Shiwasu from Six Gravity.

00:17:00.083 --> 00:17:01.500
Nice to meet you.

00:17:13.583 --> 00:17:15.583
Here's a special present for you.

00:17:15.583 --> 00:17:18.250
Don't tell anyone, okay?

00:17:18.250 --> 00:17:20.000
Tell your sister "Hi" from me.

00:17:20.000 --> 00:17:22.417
I hope she gets better soon.

00:17:23.542 --> 00:17:25.000
Thanks, Kakeru!

00:17:31.250 --> 00:17:32.958
Kakeru!

00:17:32.958 --> 00:17:35.333
Look over here!

00:17:37.125 --> 00:17:39.792
Thank you very much!

00:17:39.792 --> 00:17:43.667
This is a little sudden, but there's
something we want to share with you all.

00:17:43.667 --> 00:17:47.792
Hey, everyone, attention please!

00:17:47.792 --> 00:17:48.958
What is it?

00:17:48.958 --> 00:17:52.083
It's <i>really </i>important.

00:17:52.083 --> 00:17:54.125
What should I do?

00:17:54.125 --> 00:17:55.917
Should I say it?

00:17:55.917 --> 00:17:57.792
Should I not?

00:17:57.792 --> 00:17:59.833
What shall we do, Hajime?

00:17:59.833 --> 00:18:02.708
Shun, can we tell them already?

00:18:02.708 --> 00:18:03.958
All right.

00:18:03.958 --> 00:18:06.875
Well, go ahead, Black King.

00:18:06.875 --> 00:18:08.667
Then, let us announce--

00:18:08.667 --> 00:18:10.333
Huh? What is it?

00:18:10.333 --> 00:18:11.750
What is it?

00:18:14.750 --> 00:18:16.917
Six Gravity and--

00:18:16.917 --> 00:18:18.500
Procellarum--

00:18:27.375 --> 00:18:30.083
"Will have a joint concert!!"

00:18:30.375 --> 00:18:31.917
What?!

00:18:32.417 --> 00:18:35.500
All right! This is something
to get fired up about!

00:18:35.500 --> 00:18:37.417
We can't lose here!

00:18:37.417 --> 00:18:39.375
Just watch, Gravi!

00:18:39.375 --> 00:18:41.333
That's our line.

00:18:41.333 --> 00:18:43.958
Everyone, please support Gravi!

00:18:43.958 --> 00:18:45.708
Please support Procella, too!

00:18:48.375 --> 00:18:50.375
Sorry for surprising you.

00:18:50.375 --> 00:18:53.750
We'll give you <i>all </i>the details later.

00:18:53.750 --> 00:18:55.542
Please look forward to it.

00:18:55.542 --> 00:18:57.750
Now, to get ready for the concert,

00:18:57.750 --> 00:19:00.667
why don't we teach you this song, first?

00:19:00.667 --> 00:19:02.542
Six Gravity's new song--

00:19:02.542 --> 00:19:03.958
"Gravitic-Love"!

00:19:05.583 --> 00:19:07.208
♪ Shakin', sugar, sugar! ♪

00:19:07.208 --> 00:19:09.167
♪ Shakin', sugar, sugar! ♪

00:19:12.583 --> 00:19:14.208
♪ Shakin', sugar, sugar! ♪

00:19:14.208 --> 00:19:16.042
♪ Shakin', sugar, sugar! ♪

00:19:17.708 --> 00:19:19.708
♪ Shake it love, YES! ♪

00:19:19.708 --> 00:19:23.250
♪ I'm going crazy with longing ♪

00:19:23.250 --> 00:19:24.833
♪ Brushing back my hair ♪

00:19:24.833 --> 00:19:26.875
♪ That got wet in an instant ♪

00:19:26.875 --> 00:19:29.542
♪ Being toyed with by the warm rain ♪

00:19:29.542 --> 00:19:33.042
♪ Shall I see how far I can run? ♪

00:19:33.042 --> 00:19:35.000
♪ The prayer ♪

00:19:35.000 --> 00:19:37.000
♪ That spun out ♪

00:19:37.000 --> 00:19:39.917
♪ Connects to the future ♪

00:19:39.917 --> 00:19:40.833
♪ Overflowing ♪

00:19:40.833 --> 00:19:42.333
♪ The miracle of love ♪

00:19:42.333 --> 00:19:44.250
♪ The wonderful miracle ♪

00:19:44.250 --> 00:19:47.042
♪ The voice of these six flowers ♪

00:19:47.042 --> 00:19:49.250
♪ is released! (Shake it love, SAY!) ♪

00:19:49.250 --> 00:19:51.083
♪ Pulling toward each other (So fast!) ♪

00:19:51.083 --> 00:19:52.750
♪ That power (So vast!) ♪

00:19:52.750 --> 00:19:55.042
♪ I want it to reach you ♪

00:19:55.042 --> 00:19:56.375
♪ Don't stop the music ♪

00:19:56.375 --> 00:19:58.208
♪ High in the night sky (So high!) ♪

00:19:58.208 --> 00:20:00.292
♪ I send up my excitement (Turn round!) ♪

00:20:00.292 --> 00:20:02.750
♪ Gravitic-romantic ♪

00:20:02.750 --> 00:20:03.542
♪ Tonight ♪

00:20:03.542 --> 00:20:05.208
♪ Can't be stopped (Nonstop!) ♪

00:20:05.208 --> 00:20:07.000
♪ The impulse of love (Get down!) ♪

00:20:07.000 --> 00:20:10.125
♪ I want to mess you up ♪

00:20:10.125 --> 00:20:11.833
♪ T-T-Take it easy now! ♪

00:20:11.833 --> 00:20:13.458
♪ To embrace you ♪

00:20:13.458 --> 00:20:15.125
♪ a-a-as I feel it ♪

00:20:15.125 --> 00:20:15.875
♪ Let's dance ♪

00:20:15.875 --> 00:20:19.125
♪ And once you're captivated, kiss! ♪

00:20:19.125 --> 00:20:20.875
♪ Good love! Good love! ♪

00:20:20.875 --> 00:20:23.250
♪ Gravitic-love! ♪

00:20:23.250 --> 00:20:25.042
♪ Shakin', sugar, sugar! ♪

00:20:25.042 --> 00:20:26.958
♪ Shakin', sugar, sugar! ♪

00:20:28.125 --> 00:20:30.417
♪ Shake it love, YES! ♪

00:20:36.333 --> 00:20:38.000
That was so cool!

00:20:39.417 --> 00:20:43.583
♪ Good love! Good love! Gravitic-love! ♪

00:20:43.583 --> 00:20:45.292
Welcome back, Syunpei!

00:20:45.292 --> 00:20:47.250
Thanks! I was waiting for you!

00:20:47.250 --> 00:20:50.500
Hey, let me borrow your CD. The Gravi one.

00:20:51.875 --> 00:20:53.375
What is it, Syunpei?

00:20:53.375 --> 00:20:55.625
Don't tell me you're interested in them now?

00:20:55.625 --> 00:20:57.542
I just wanted to listen to it a little.

00:20:57.542 --> 00:21:01.000
Oh? Did you realize how great
Kakerun was at the handshake event?

00:21:01.000 --> 00:21:03.292
That's not it...

00:21:03.292 --> 00:21:06.417
Well? Well? How was the handshake event?

00:21:06.417 --> 00:21:09.875
What was Kakerun like?

00:21:09.875 --> 00:21:11.500
Okay.

00:21:11.500 --> 00:21:13.875
What do you mean, "okay"?

00:21:13.875 --> 00:21:15.500
Is this the merch I asked you to get?

00:21:15.500 --> 00:21:17.333
Don't touch that!

00:21:17.333 --> 00:21:19.000
That's mine!

00:21:22.083 --> 00:21:25.792
Wh-Wh-Wh-What is this?!

00:21:25.792 --> 00:21:27.583
--Hey!
--You're so loud.

00:21:27.583 --> 00:21:28.750
What's the deal with this?!

00:21:28.750 --> 00:21:30.500
Explain yourself!

00:21:30.500 --> 00:21:32.708
It's a long story.

00:21:32.708 --> 00:21:33.750
I don't wanna tell it.

00:21:33.750 --> 00:21:35.375
Please, Syunpi!

00:21:35.375 --> 00:21:36.542
Please tell me!

00:21:36.542 --> 00:21:37.708
Come on, Syunpi!

00:21:37.708 --> 00:21:38.917
--Please!
--Don't wanna!

00:21:38.917 --> 00:21:41.625
--I'll never ask you for anything again!
--Hurry up and let me borrow your CD!

00:21:53.292 --> 00:21:55.958
<i>Staying focused all year round</i>

00:21:55.958 --> 00:21:58.708
<i>Chase both hares,</i>
<i>the pen and the sword, and catch both</i>

00:21:58.708 --> 00:22:01.000
<i>Part-time job, classes, singing and dance lessons</i>

00:22:01.000 --> 00:22:04.208
<i>Show the vector of where</i>
<i>I'm going with an arrow, fly high!</i>

00:22:04.208 --> 00:22:06.792
<i>It's an emergency! A test is coming up</i>

00:22:06.792 --> 00:22:09.417
<i>Oh no, oh no! This shift is bad</i>

00:22:09.417 --> 00:22:11.750
<i>As a present to myself at a time like this, </i>

00:22:11.750 --> 00:22:15.750
<i>I head to one of my favorite places today</i>

00:22:15.750 --> 00:22:19.458
<i>At an unassuming cafe on a back street</i>

00:22:20.458 --> 00:22:25.125
<i>Where adding a vanilla ice cream costs 200 yen</i>

00:22:25.125 --> 00:22:31.167
<i>Quietly peeking into my wallet</i>

00:22:31.167 --> 00:22:35.833
<i>My hand shakes. It's time to make a decision--</i>

00:22:35.833 --> 00:22:37.375
<i>"Don't call me middle class!"</i>

00:22:37.375 --> 00:22:40.208
<i>Let's do our best tomorrow, too</i>

00:22:40.208 --> 00:22:43.375
<i>I like you who likes me when I do my best</i>

00:22:43.375 --> 00:22:46.500
<i>If I'm gonna hold my knees</i>

00:22:46.500 --> 00:22:48.792
<i>Then I might as well turn a somersault like that</i>

00:22:48.792 --> 00:22:51.042
<i>Winter nights when I'm numb with cold</i>

00:22:51.042 --> 00:22:54.125
<i>And summer vacation</i>
<i>with my sweat-drenched T-shirts</i>

00:22:54.125 --> 00:22:57.083
<i>They might not be too bad</i>

00:22:57.083 --> 00:23:11.917
<i>Rising spirits glittering</i>

00:23:11.917 --> 00:23:12.875
"Episode 2: Glasswork Heart"

00:23:12.875 --> 00:23:14.667
"Episode 2: Glasswork Heart"
I became a member of Procella

00:23:14.667 --> 00:23:17.042
"Episode 2: Glasswork Heart"
and did various things,

00:23:17.042 --> 00:23:18.458
"Episode 2: Glasswork Heart"
but when I go back to my hometown,

00:23:18.458 --> 00:23:19.833
"Episode 2: Glasswork Heart"
I still have to practice with the track team

00:23:19.833 --> 00:23:21.833
"Episode 2: Glasswork Heart"
and study, of course.

00:23:22.833 --> 00:23:25.667
No matter how much
time I have, it's not enough.

00:23:25.667 --> 00:23:28.292
How does everyone else manage it?

00:23:28.292 --> 00:23:32.667
You, Yoru, please tell me!

00:23:32.667 --> 00:23:35.500
Next time, "Glasswork Heart"!

00:23:35.500 --> 00:23:42.059
I, Iku Kannaduki, will definitely be
successful as an idol and on the track team!
